          "update_time": 1794669968.681,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "The clearest quantitative result so far is the coefficient bound: the squared Jacobi couplings grow at most like \\((\\log n)^2\\). It feeds directly into a proved finite-chain error bound. The chain is also exactly Gaussian quadrature, so its tensor interpretation does not by itself establish a computational advantage.\n"
            ]
          },
