          "create_time": 1794670034.116,
          "update_time": 1794670037.629,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "The drafts support a useful distinction for brainstorming. Jacobi/Volterra provides the strongest current link from source structure to an error bound; QTT provides a fixed-box rank bound; and exact cell integration gives an error bound uniform over real height. None yet provides a new zero-exclusion estimate. Known colliding controls even satisfy the Volterra coefficient bound.\n\nChat registration now works after a narrowly scoped recorder compatibility fix; its checks passed. I’m saving the synthesis and a short list of analytical directions.\n"
            ]
          },
